                <div class="wrap wrap_story">
<!-- Article Header Section: Title, Deck, Category/Date -->
<section class="section section_article-header">
    <div class="article-header">
        <h1 class="article-header__title">
            The Day Playboy Bunnies Went On Strike        </h1>
        
                <p class="article-header__deck">
            They walked out of the Chicago club for better working conditions, but it wasn't what it seemed.        </p>
                
        <div class="article-header__meta">
                        <span class="article-header__category">
                <a href="https://www.playboy.com/read/classics">Classics</a>
            </span>
            <span class="article-header__separator">•</span>
                        <span class="article-header__date">May 1, 2026</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Full-Width Featured Image -->
<section class="section section_article-image">
    <div class="article-image" data-pb-lightbox data-full="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_VIP_Fall_Bunny_Lib_by_Bill_Frantz_01_w2-scaled-e1777566448395.jpg" style="--image: url('https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_VIP_Fall_Bunny_Lib_by_Bill_Frantz_01_w2-scaled-e1777566448395.jpg'); --image-m: url('https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_VIP_Fall_Bunny_Lib_by_Bill_Frantz_01_w2-scaled-e1777566448395-720x698.jpg');">
    </div>
        <div class="article-image__caption">
                By Bill Frantz            </div>
    </section>

<!-- Byline Section -->
<section class="section section_article-byline">
    <div class="article-byline">
                <div class="article-byline__item">
            <span class="article-byline__label">Written by</span>
                        <a href="https://www.playboy.com/read/author/brittney-mcnamara" class="article-byline__name">BRITTNEY MCNAMARA</a>
                    </div>
                
                
            </div>
</section>

<!-- Story Content -->
<section class="section section_story">
    <div class="story">
        <div class="story__content">
            <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd">
<html><body><p>In the 1970s, workplace protest was in. According to <em><a href="https://jacobin.com/2021/01/1970s-decade-strike-workers-labor-history">Jacobin</a></em>, there were 5,716 strikes involving 3 million workers in the year 1970 alone, kicking off a decade of labor revolt, often led by young people who refused to accept the status quo. </p>



<p>It was against this backdrop that Playboy Club Bunnies in Chicago walked off the job in June 1975. On a Wednesday, the club Bunnies went on strike for more fair <a href="https://www.playboy.com/read/sex-relationships/she-made-1-million-in-3-hours-on-onlyfans-then-the-headaches">working conditions</a> and equality in the clubs. Their demands were simple: they were pushing back on unfair policies that banned them from using their full names on the job, dating club members, and from having a key to the club (the term for the cards club members carried to gain entry). As part of their cause, the women on strike wrote a letter to <em>Playboy</em> founder Hugh Hefner outlining their concern:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="677" height="1024" data-id="59014" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-677x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59014" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-677x1024.jpg 677w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-198x300.jpg 198w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-768x1162.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-1015x1536.jpg 1015w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-1354x2048.jpg 1354w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-1200x1815.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-720x1089.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-600x908.jpg 600w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_08-scaled.jpg 1692w" sizes="(max-width: 677px) 100vw, 677px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="677" height="1024" data-id="59015" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-677x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59015" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-677x1024.jpg 677w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-198x300.jpg 198w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-768x1161.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-1016x1536.jpg 1016w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-1355x2048.jpg 1355w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-1200x1814.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-720x1089.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-600x907.jpg 600w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_07-scaled.jpg 1693w" sizes="(max-width: 677px) 100vw, 677px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="681" height="1024" data-id="59016" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-681x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59016" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-681x1024.jpg 681w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-199x300.jpg 199w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-768x1156.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-1021x1536.jpg 1021w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-1361x2048.jpg 1361w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-1200x1806.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-720x1083.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-600x903.jpg 600w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_02-scaled.jpg 1701w" sizes="(max-width: 681px) 100vw, 681px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>
</figure>



<p>&#8220;We love being Playboy Bunnies and most of the time we love you, but there are times when we think you are a Male Chauvinist Rabbit,&#8221; the letter read, according to an article about the 1975 strike by Patty Farmer in <em>Playboy</em>&#8216;s November 2017 issue. &#8220;While you are, admittedly, the leader of sexual liberation, you have set the cause of Bunny Lib back 10 years. Our private lives should be our own&#8230;.We intend to let the outside world know we are unhappy. We have nothing to lose but our tails and our ears.&#8221;</p>



<p>So, they took to the streets, picketing the club with signs declaring their demands&mdash;and they won. Hefner wrote back to the Bunnies acquiescing to their requests, making &#8220;Bunny Lib a reality instead of a slogan,&#8221; as he wrote in his response to the his employees. The club rules would be relaxed to meet the more free swinging vibe of the &#8217;70s.</p><div class="aplace"><div class="htlad-story-inline"></div></div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59017" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-768x511.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-1536x1023.jpg 1536w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-2048x1364.jpg 2048w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-1200x799.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-720x480.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_04-600x400.jpg 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>



<p>This would be fantastic lore&mdash;a labor rights win and a great story to tell to kick off Labor History Month this May. Unfortunately, it&#8217;s all a ruse. </p>



<p>The Bunnies did walk out of the Chicago club, and they did carry signs calling for &#8220;Bunny Lib.&#8221; They did not like the policies that limited them from dating club members or that barred them from having club keys. But they did not lobby for better working conditions of their own accord. The so-called protest was planned by Victor Lownes, <em>Playboy&#8217;s</em> longtime promotional director, as a publicity stunt, a way to update club policy and gain favorable attention while doing it. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="685" height="1024" data-id="59023" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-685x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59023" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-685x1024.jpg 685w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-201x300.jpg 201w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-768x1148.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-1028x1536.jpg 1028w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-1370x2048.jpg 1370w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-1200x1793.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-720x1076.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-600x897.jpg 600w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/F_1711_1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_03_w2-2-scaled.jpg 1713w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="694" height="1024" data-id="59019" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-694x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59019" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-694x1024.jpg 694w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-203x300.jpg 203w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-768x1133.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1042x1536.jpg 1042w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1389x2048.jpg 1389w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1200x1770.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-720x1062.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-600x885.jpg 600w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_by_Ken_Frantz_01-scaled.jpg 1736w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 694px) 100vw, 694px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>
</figure>



<p>According to Farmer&#8217;s 2017 article on the walkout, the Playboy Club developed strict policy around Bunny behavior when it opened in 1960 because it was under heavy scrutiny from the city of Chicago and the Catholic Church&mdash;a powerful force in the city. Club founders worried that they would be shut down for prostitution if a Bunny went home with a club member, or engaged in anything other than a strictly professional relationship. To prevent that, Club Bunnies had to be friendly but not <em>too</em> friendly, couldn&#8217;t use their last names at the club, and could never, ever date or hang out with a club member outside the club. &#8220;Even if you met someone outside who happened to be a key-holder, you had to let [management] know,&#8221; former Bunny and strike &#8220;leader&#8221; Sharon Gwin told Farmer.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="684" src="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1024x684.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-59021" srcset="https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1024x684.jpg 1024w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-768x513.jpg 768w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1536x1026.jpg 1536w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-2048x1368.jpg 2048w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-1200x802.jpg 1200w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-720x481.jpg 720w, https://www.playboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1975_06_Bunny_Lib_Protest_by_Ken_Frantz_01-600x401.jpg 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo by Ken Frantz</figcaption></figure>



<p>But by 1975, those rules felt outdated&mdash;even regressive. Bunnies wanted to have access to the clubs in the same way members did, and they wanted to make their own decisions about their personal lives. &#8220;They were protecting us, but we were all adults,&#8221; Laura Lyons, a Bunny and Playmate, told Farmer. So, there was unrest among club employees because of these policies, and Bunnies did want change to give them more agency on the job. But it wasn&#8217;t the Bunnies banding together to demand better labor conditions that made change, it was a plot devised by Lownes to bring club policies into the present day, and to get good press while doing it. The rules did change, and benefitted employees. But that it was actually the boss who crafted a faux-strike? That&#8217;s a big Bunny bummer.</p><div class="aplace"><div class="htlad-story-inline"></div></div>



<p></p>
</body></html>
        </div>
